            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Etingof"} Etingof
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BenZviNadler09"} Ben-Zvi &amp; Nadler 09
          %p
            The most efficient and intuitive way to define the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/six+operations"} six operations
            on D-modules is to transfer them from
            %span.newWikiWord
              Ω-modules
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%CE%A9-modules"} ?
            (i.e., modules over the differential graded algebra of differential forms) using
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koszul+duality"} Koszul duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/six+operations"} six operations
            on
            %span.newWikiWord
              Ω-modules
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%CE%A9-modules"} ?
            can be defined in the standard way using the fact that differential forms can be pulled back, unlike differential operators. See the article
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koszul+duality"} Koszul duality
            for more information.
